{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01XjZ9HT3i2UMuwALeh5JgXq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"API Error: Stream idle timeout - partial response received"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa9e45a4c38e6ebcd (use SendMessage with to: 'aa9e45a4c38e6ebcd' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 0\ntool_uses: 2\nduration_ms: 309505</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32aa5972-b92a-4580-b5c5-f0297ce83ccb","uuid":"20ae7651-9724-4002-b2fb-da6b18c2af73","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:10:14.634Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write a complete markdown answers file for the payments-system frontend system design topic, section 05: \"Performance & Core Web Vitals\".\n\n## Output file\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/05-performance-core-web-vitals.md`\n\n## Questions to answer (from the design doc)\n\n### Core questions:\n1. Stripe.js is a ~300KB third-party script. When and how should you load it, and why does Stripe's own documentation recommend loading it on every page of your site rather than only on the checkout page? What are the performance trade-offs of each approach?\n2. How does injecting a Stripe Elements iframe into the DOM affect Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS), and what CSS techniques do you use to prevent the card input from causing layout shifts when it mounts?\n3. Describe your bundle-splitting strategy for a checkout page. Which chunks are critical path, which are deferred, and how do you decide what to inline in the HTML vs. load asynchronously?\n4. What is the impact of third-party payment SDKs (Stripe, PayPal button, Apple Pay, Google Pay) on your checkout page's Total Blocking Time (TBT) and Interaction to Next Paint (INP)? How do you load these without blocking the main thread?\n5. How would you optimize the Time to Interactive (TTI) for a checkout page that requires: authentication state check, cart data fetch, Stripe.js load, and address form render — all before the user can type a card number?\n6. Describe how you would use resource hints (`preconnect`, `prefetch`, `preload`) specifically for a checkout page that loads Stripe.js, Google Fonts for the branded card input, and a product image CDN.\n7. What are the trade-offs between server-side rendering (SSR), static generation, and client-side rendering for a checkout page? Which approach do you use, and how does it affect Time to First Byte (TTFB) and the \"page is interactive\" moment?\n\n### Deep questions:\n1. A/B test results show that your checkout page has a 15% higher bounce rate on 3G mobile connections compared to competitors. Your LCP is 4.2s. Walk through a systematic performance audit: which tools do you use, what hypotheses do you form, and which specific optimizations do you implement for the Stripe SDK loading, hero image, and above-the-fold form render?\n2. Stripe Elements renders inside an iframe, which means the browser must establish a separate network connection to `js.stripe.com`. Model the exact sequence of DNS lookup, TCP handshake, TLS negotiation, and iframe load for a user on a 50ms-latency mobile connection. Where are the optimization opportunities, and what is the irreducible minimum latency floor you cannot engineer around?\n3. You are asked to implement a \"one-click checkout\" experience (similar to Shop Pay or Amazon 1-Click) where returning users can complete a purchase in under 2 seconds. Describe the full performance architecture: what is pre-fetched on the product page, what is pre-loaded on hover/tap, how is the PaymentIntent pre-created, and what is the critical rendering path once the user clicks \"Buy Now\"?\n\n## Answer format (for EVERY question)\n\nUse this exact structure per question:\n\n```\n### Q: [question text verbatim]\n\n**Problem framing:** …\n\n**Approach:** …\n\n[optional Mermaid diagram in approach if it aids clarity]\n\n**Tradeoffs:** …\n```\n\n## File header format\n\n```markdown\n# 05 — Performance & Core Web Vitals\n\n> [brief section intro sentence]\n\n## Core\n[7 questions]\n\n## Deep\n[3 questions]\n```\n\n## Quality bar\n- Interview-depth answers (senior/staff level). Be specific and technical.\n- Reference real browser APIs, real Stripe APIs, real Web Vitals metrics.\n- For Core Web Vitals questions: cite specific metrics (LCP, CLS, TBT, INP, FID, TTFB) with typical thresholds (good/needs improvement/poor).\n- For Stripe questions: be accurate about how Stripe.js works (preconnects to js.stripe.com, q.stripe.com; Elements iframe origin is js.stripe.com; stripe.com recommends loading on all pages for fraud detection fingerprinting).\n- Include Mermaid diagrams where they genuinely add value (e.g., the network connection sequence for the Deep Q2).\n- Tradeoffs section should be non-trivial — compare real alternatives.\n- Do not use fluffy filler. Every sentence should be actionable interview content.\n\n## Reference style\nLook at the existing answer files to match the writing style:\n- `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.md`\n- `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.md`\n\nRead those files first to match their tone and depth, then write the new file.\n","agentId":"aa9e45a4c38e6ebcd","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"API Error: Stream idle timeout - partial response received"}],"resolvedModel":"blackboxai/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5","totalDurationMs":309505,"totalTokens":0,"totalToolUseCount":2,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":null,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":null,"iterations":null,"speed":null},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,